 "result_text": "`get_schema` should no longer crash on Junos replies. I haven't run it or any tests, and I didn't try it against a Junos device or the gist reply.\n\nThe fix is in `GetSchemaReply._parsing_hook` in `ncclient/operations/retrieve.py`. It still looks for `data` in the `ietf-netconf-monitoring` namespace first. If that finds nothing, it takes the first child of the reply root whose tag is `data`, whatever its namespace. If there is no `data` element at all, `_data` stays `None` instead of raising `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'text'`.\n\nI used a plain loop over the children rather than the `{*}data` wildcard because that wildcard needs Python 3.8 or later.",
